in world war one both sides tried to  recruit other nations to join them and  tip the balance in their favor the  ottomans the italians and the romanians  being some of those enticed into joining  the conflict yet spain a country of 20  million people at the time managed to  stay neutral throughout the entire thing  and given that both sides were trying to  bribe up new allies why did spain sit it  out why did spain stay neutral in the  first world war before getting specific  it's important to know that as of 1914  spain wasn't having a good time its  economy was sluggish it had barely  industrialized it was deeply divided  internally and militarily things were  worse just before the war the spanish  had suffered military humiliation in  morocco when they tried to expand their  influence there in 1909 they did manage  to defeat the rebelling moroccans  eventually but that wasn't until after  numerous defeats in the sending of tens  of thousands of troops to morocco to  defeat one twentieth of their number and  so when franz ferdinand visited sarajevo  to try his hand at being assassinated it  wasn't long until world war one was well  on its way spain immediately declared  its neutrality and wanted nothing to do  with the war and the overriding reason  was simple it felt that it had nothing  to gain the previous spanish-american  war had taught spain that warfare was  painful even if the fighting stayed away  from the homeland and for many the  potential gains weren't even that great  if they joined the central powers then  spain could have potentially gained  gibraltar or something but that would  involve spain having to go toe-to-toe  with the well-equipped and well-trained  anton troops and given the previous  disaster in morocco spain wasn't ready  for that and if spain had joined the  anton then it may have been able to gain  some possessions in africa or  potentially in the pacific but the  benefits would have been little and  there was the potential for retaliation  furthermore spain had no quarrel with  germany or austria-hungary nor did it  have any feelings of kinship towards  serbia or belgium which gave them no  reason to join and even if the  government had wanted to pick a side and  ignored the risks there was the second  reason they didn't join political  instability spain's people were  extremely divided between the  assassination of the archduke and the  signing of the treaty of versailles  spain had nine governments headed by  four different prime ministers  each had preferences towards the ontart  or the central powers but all of them  preferred neutrality for the third  reason spain stayed out of the war cash  being neutral meant that you could sell  stuff to both sides and spain did very  well for itself doing just that it sold  food and raw materials to the untaunted  chemicals and textiles to the central  powers the influx of money saw spain's  industrialization speed up and spain's  gold reserves increased massively and  the fourth reason was that nobody else  wanted spain to join the central power  was wanted in neutral spain which could  be used for espionage and some trade and  the anton wanted spain to stay out of  the war since they didn't want to share  any of the potential spoils in africa  with them and thus neutrality was a  simple risk-free option but there were  some issues germany sank spanish  shipping which led to prime minister  alvaro de  are getting fired when he tried to  denounce germany for it and spain was  also threatened with invasion by the  anton when german troops fled into  spanish guinea and they didn't do much  about it of course spain managed to  maneuver through these issues and stay  neutral throughout the war and you would  assume that the massive influx of money  into spain would make the lives of  spaniards better but you would be wrong  workers saw no wage rises which led to  more and more of them turning to  anarchism or socialism to help and when  it became clear to farmers that it was  much more profitable to sell food to  italy or france than it was to the  spanish there were food shortages too  and so it won't surprise you that even  though spain avoided the horrors of  world war one it entered the post-war  world an even more divided nation but  that was a problem for another time i  hope you enjoyed this episode and thank  you for watching with a special thanks  to my patrons james bissonette kelly  moneymaker corso wolfe adam stalter  jerry lamdin jordan longley rod d martin  lion hockey gustav swan spencer  lightfoot captain cydog winston k wood  boogery wiggly marvin castle aaron the  white words about books podcast commun  yoon matthew shipley maxon flutio alex  schwinn maggie patzkowski marcus asner  the mug whopper corey turner anthony  beckett coppertone spinning three plates  charles the first ben evanson and  scottish trekkie
 

